From: LxnChan <lingxuanning@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: attach loaded CRT and win32u before ARM64EC dependency cycles

SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-or-later

The iDeck PE farm promotes delay imports to eager imports. A GUI cycle
can initialize comctl32 while gdi32/user32 are still in progress, before
their win32u dependency is attached. Its first NtGdiCreateBitmap then
branches through a NULL __wine_syscall_dispatcher.

The same eager graph can reach an application-local version.dll from
shell32 before advapi32's last dependency, msvcrt, initializes. MelonLoader's
NativeAOT proxy calls LookupPrivilegeValueW at attach time; its _wcsicmp
then dereferences the still-NULL MSVCRT_locale.

After kernel32 bootstrap, attach an already loaded msvcrt and win32u before
walking other nodes. These builtins depend only on ntdll/kernel32. Keep
loader locking, recursion guards, pinning, activation contexts and failure
propagation in process_attach. Do not load either DLL into processes that
do not need them, or change other architectures' attach order.

--- a/dlls/ntdll/loader.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/loader.c
@@ -2224,8 +2224,34 @@
     if (lpReserved) wm->ldr.LoadCount = -1;  /* pin it if imported by the main exe */
     if (wm->ldr.ActivationContext) RtlActivateActivationContext( 0, wm->ldr.ActivationContext, &cookie );

+#ifdef __arm64ec__
+    /* The PE farm promotes delay imports to ordinary imports to avoid x64
+     * delay thunks in the ARM64EC JIT copy. The resulting GUI dependency
+     * cycles can reach application-local version.dll (MelonLoader) before
+     * advapi32's msvcrt dependency has initialized MSVCRT_locale, or reach
+     * comctl32 before win32u sets __wine_syscall_dispatcher. Initialize
+     * these ntdll/kernel32-only leaves first. Do not load new modules or
+     * attach them during emulator / kernel32 bootstrap. The current node
+     * is already marked in progress, preserving reentrant cycle guards. */
+    if (imports_fixup_done)
+    {
+        WINE_MODREF *kernel32 = find_basename_module( L"kernel32.dll" );
+        WINE_MODREF *msvcrt = find_basename_module( L"msvcrt.dll" );
+        WINE_MODREF *win32u = find_basename_module( L"win32u.dll" );
+
+        if (kernel32 && (kernel32->ldr.Flags & LDR_PROCESS_ATTACHED))
+        {
+            if (msvcrt && msvcrt != wm && (msvcrt->ldr.Flags & LDR_WINE_INTERNAL))
+                status = process_attach( msvcrt->ldr.DdagNode, lpReserved );
+            if (status == STATUS_SUCCESS && win32u && win32u != wm)
+                status = process_attach( win32u->ldr.DdagNode, lpReserved );
+        }
+    }
+#endif
+
     /* Recursively attach all DLLs this one depends on */
-    status = walk_node_dependencies( node, lpReserved, process_attach );
+    if (status == STATUS_SUCCESS)
+        status = walk_node_dependencies( node, lpReserved, process_attach );

     if (!wm->ldr.InInitializationOrderLinks.Flink)
         InsertTailList(&NtCurrentTeb()->Peb->LdrData->InInitializationOrderModuleList,
